  <section class="page-shell py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-anica-signal">Pipeline</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-black tracking-[0.06em] text-anica-ink">How it works</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-anica-steel">
        MotionLoom keeps the editable source as plain DSL. A future Anica panel can expose After Effects-style controls while preserving the graph underneath.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-3xl border-2 border-anica-ink bg-anica-cream p-5 shadow-[6px_6px_0_#11120d]">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-anica-steel">1. Parse</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-anica-ink">Slider values update curve keyframes, timings, and node attributes in the DSL text.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-3xl border-2 border-anica-ink bg-anica-cream p-5 shadow-[6px_6px_0_#11120d]">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-anica-steel">2. Compile</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-anica-ink">The same source can be opened, edited, diffed, generated by agents, or compiled by the renderer.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-3xl border-2 border-anica-ink bg-anica-cream p-5 shadow-[6px_6px_0_#11120d]">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-anica-steel">3. Execute</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-anica-ink">Scene graphs render through MotionLoom WASM; native renderer errors are surfaced instead of hidden by a browser fallback.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-shell py-16 text-center">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl rounded-[2.5rem] border-2 border-anica-ink bg-anica-ink px-6 py-14 text-anica-paper soft-panel md:px-12">
